# passe probe script: re-capture the Voyager GraphQL queryIds used by
# linkedin_posts_lib.fetch_person_comments when LinkedIn rotates them.
#
# WHEN TO RUN THIS
#     fetch_posts.py starts returning http 400 on the comments fetch, OR
#     fetch_person_comments returns "could not resolve fsd_profile URN" for
#     profiles that previously worked.
#
# HOW TO RUN
#     1. Make sure you're logged into LinkedIn in the debug Chrome on port 9223:
#          chrome-debug         # or however you launch Chrome with --remote-debugging-port=9223
#          # then manually log into LinkedIn in that window if needed
#
#     2. Replace the target profile URL below with any person's /recent-activity/comments/
#        page — the probe just needs LinkedIn to issue a real comments-on-others
#        GraphQL call so we can capture the queryId.
#
#     3. Run the probe:
#          PASSE_CDP=http://localhost:9223 passe run comments-probe.passe
#
#     4. Extract the new queryIds from /tmp/comments-capture.jsonl:
#          python3 -c "
#          import json
#          for line in open('/tmp/comments-capture.jsonl'):
#              r=json.loads(line)
#              u=r.get('url','')
#              if 'voyager/api/graphql' in u and 'voyagerFeedDashProfileUpdates' in u:
#                  print('COMMENTS_QUERY_ID =', u.split('queryId=')[1])
#              if 'voyagerIdentityDashProfiles.' in u and 'memberIdentity' in u:
#                  print('PROFILES_QUERY_ID =', u.split('queryId=')[1])
#          "
#
#     5. Paste the new hashes into linkedin_posts_lib.py constants
#        PROFILES_QUERY_ID and COMMENTS_QUERY_ID at the top of the file.
#
# ALTERNATIVE: if you don't have passe installed, you can re-capture manually via
# Chrome DevTools: open linkedin.com → DevTools → Network tab → filter for
# "voyager/api/graphql" → visit a profile's /recent-activity/comments/ page →
# copy the queryId from the request URL.

goto https://www.linkedin.com/feed/
wait 2
eval (()=>{const s=document.querySelector('header'); return 'logged_in='+(s?'yes':'no')})()
capture --bodies /tmp/comments-capture.jsonl
goto https://www.linkedin.com/in/REPLACE_WITH_ANY_PROFILE_SLUG/recent-activity/comments/
wait-idle 20
wait 3
eval document.title
